{# The page shown when a request cannot go on and nothing may be sent to a client (RFC 9700 §4.1,
   RP-Initiated Logout §4), in the locale of the request. "error" is a code: the "error" of the protocol,
   or one of the constants of AuthorizationResponder and of the controllers; the codes this page can
   explain get their sentence, any other the general one. "description", when there is one, is the
   error_description of the protocol: what the developer of the application needs to fix their request
   (RFC 6749 §4.1.2.1), in the language of the specification. Overridable by an application under
   templates/bundles/BeffroiBundle/. #}
{% extends '@Beffroi/layout.html.twig' %}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}

{# This page is a refusal and not a page of this provider: the request stops here, there is nothing on it
   to come back to and nothing of a person to read, whatever route it was asked on. An application whose
   layout serves the pages of the account in a skeleton of their own reads this to serve a refusal in the
   skeleton of a page that asks one thing and carries nothing else, rather than as one more page of an
   account that nobody is signed in to. The name is the bundle's, as the functions an overridden layout
   reads are (beffroi_tenant), because it is what a page of the bundle says to a layout of an application
   and not a variable a page is rendered with. #}
{% set beffroi_refusal = true %}

{% set explained_errors = ['unknown_interaction', 'interaction_expired', 'interaction_completed', 'invalid_csrf_token', 'invalid_request', 'login_required', 'no_login_to_begin', 'too_many_requests', 'enrolment_ticket_refused', 'saml_request_refused', 'saml_logout_refused', 'saml_upstream_sign_on_refused', 'saml_assertion_refused'] %}

{% block title %}{{ 'error.title'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <p data-error="{{ error }}">{{ (error in explained_errors ? 'error.' ~ error : 'error.default')|trans }}</p>
    {% if description is not null %}
        <p data-description><code>{{ error }}</code>: {{ description }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {# The way out of the one refusal that has one here. A page of the account refused to a browser that
       holds no session is a page it may read once it has one, and the home of the account is where this
       provider offers the login and comes back from it (AccountController, LoginTarget): the link is that
       login, and the refusal is not a page somebody is left on. The other codes are refusals of a request
       a client made, and what they are answered by is that client and nothing of this provider.

       It is the home of the account and never "/": the root belongs to the application that installs the
       bundle, which serves the pages of the issuer under the path it imports them at. #}
    {% if error == 'login_required' %}
        <nav><a href="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account') }}" data-sign-in>{{ 'error.sign_in'|trans }}</a></nav>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
